# ***************
# Filename: synth.ys
# Author: Paul Barcelona
# Description: Common Yosys script for every IP. Reads the design
#   (generated read_design.ys), elaborates, optimizes, infers memories
#   into block RAM, packs multipliers into DSP48 and synthesizes to
#   Xilinx 7-series primitives. Hierarchical utilization is reported.
# Date: 2026-09-29
#
# Working directory is build/yosys/<ip>; every result is written here.

# ---- 1. Read sources and set the top module ----
script read_design.ys

# ---- 2. Compile / elaborate to RTL cells ----
proc
opt_expr
opt_clean
check -assert
tee -o pre_synth.rpt stat

# ---- 3. Technology independent optimization ----
opt -full
wreduce
peepopt
opt_clean

# ---- 3b. Logic depth estimate (Yosys has no static timing engine) ----
# Longest topological path per module before technology mapping. Flops
# and memories break paths (-noff). Keep depth small (about <= 10) for
# 100 MHz closure; use Vivado or nextpnr for real static timing.
tee -o logic_depth.rpt ltp -noff

# ---- 4. Memories -> BRAM/LUTRAM, multipliers -> DSP48E1, LUT6 map ----
# Hierarchy is kept (no -flatten) so utilization can be reported per module.
synth_xilinx -family xc7 -noiopad -noclkbuf -run :map_ffs
opt -full
synth_xilinx -family xc7 -noiopad -noclkbuf -run map_ffs:

# ---- 5. Clean up and check ----
opt_clean -purge
check

# ---- 6. Reports and netlist ----
tee -o utilization_hier.rpt stat -tech xilinx -width
tee -o utilization_flat.rpt stat -tech xilinx
write_verilog -noattr netlist.v
write_json netlist.json
